{number: 16}
{title: Fairest Lord Jesus}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Fairest Lord [G] Jesus, [C] Ruler of [F] all [C] nature,
[C] O Thou of [F] God and [C] man the [G] Son,
[C] Thee will I [F] cherish, [C] Thee will I [G] honor,
[Am] Thou, my soul's [F] glory, [C] joy, [G] and [C] crown.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Fair are the [G] meadows, [C] fairer still the [F] wood-[C] lands,
[C] Robed in the [F] blooming [C] garb of [G] spring:
[C] Jesus is [F] fairer, [C] Jesus is [G] purer,
[Am] Who makes the [F] woeful [C] heart [G] to [C] sing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Fair is the [G] sunshine, [C] fairer still the [F] moon-[C] light,
[C] And all the [F] twinkling, [C] starry [G] host:
[C] Jesus shines [F] brighter, [C] Jesus shines [G] purer,
[Am] Than all the [F] angels [C] heaven [G] can [C] boast.
{end_of_verse}
